// InstallSpec Install intent template (docs/04-install-spec.md §5). Any string value may carry template references — `{var:name}` (resolved from the target's `targets[].vars`), `{index}`, `{machine_id}`, `{serial}`, `{bmc_address}`, `{label:key}` — expanded per machine at submission; unrecognized `{...}` sequences stay literal, so shell `${...}` and JSON snippets pass through untouched. base64 script bodies are opaque and never templated. Resolution runs at submission per machine; a missing binding rejects the whole request (422 SCHEMA_UNRESOLVED_VAR), a malformed address after substitution rejects with SCHEMA_INVALID_ADDRESS.
